1. A computer-implemented method for opening a cloud-based document in a native local application, the method comprising:

- receiving, by a computing device, a request to open a cloud document, the request including a document identifier and a user identifier;
- using the document identifier and the user identifier to locate a server file associated with the cloud document and accessible to the user;
- generating or retrieving a local copy of the server file on the computing device;
- determining, based at least in part on a file type, format, metadata, or content of the server file or the local copy, a list of document processing applications installed on or available to the computing device that are compatible with the cloud document;
- presenting the list of compatible document processing applications to the user;
- receiving a selection of one application from the list of compatible document processing applications; and
- opening the local copy of the server file in the selected application.

A computer-implemented method performed by an electronic device, the method comprising:

receiving, by a first local application executing on the electronic device, an open-document request identifying a document accessible to the first local application;

in response to receiving the open-document request, forwarding, by the first local application, at least a portion of the open-document request to a second local application executing on the electronic device;

receiving, by the first local application from the second local application, information identifying one or more candidate document-processing applications installed on the electronic device, each of the one or more candidate document-processing applications being capable of processing a file type associated with the document;

selecting, from among the one or more candidate document-processing applications, a selected document-processing application; and

causing the selected document-processing application to open a local file corresponding to the document on the electronic device.
